                                "sense_id": "c2130d36-64b3-3e04-a824-cc5ec362fa55",
                                "text": "[…] and the measurement and correction of astigmia is one of the chief functions of the optometrist."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "475a9c1a-9c9c-4546-b0c6-975809dc4465",
                                "sense_id": "c2130d36-64b3-3e04-a824-cc5ec362fa55",
                                "text": "Astigmia of the whole eye […] is the resultant of the special astigmia of all four refracting surfaces, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e495b1d3-34c8-45d4-9721-b57e8a0ce5b4",
                                "sense_id": "c2130d36-64b3-3e04-a824-cc5ec362fa55",
                                "text": "Regular astigmia must be considered congenital, as a rule."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ae3608a-72bf-4b26-9796-82b109ccc9fd",
                                "sense_id": "c2130d36-64b3-3e04-a824-cc5ec362fa55",
                                "text": "When the corneal astigmia is direct, and about 0.75 D., we may expect to find an almost total absence of astigmia by subjective examination."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
